A command's taken playback id does not switch again.

When the chain takes a command's playback id it clears it in the card's state
(clearCuePlayback), and that render runs the switching effect once more for the
same clip. dsh-pet left that run to the chain's check for a switch still
loading the clip. When the clip had already been fetched and decoded before the
render, the run started a new switch: the clip was fetched again and its command
answered cancelled. The effect now skips the run that only clears the id; a
replay of the same clip still bumps seq and plays.

